1. This is the FPGA Synthesis and Implementation Directory.
2. Steps
   -- Install Vivado and ensure that 'vivado' is in the path. (vivado -help)
   -- Run the command: vivado -mode batch -source ./syn.tcl
      -- This will do FPGA synthesis, P&R and generates bit stream.
   -- Open Vivado GUI
      vivado &
      Create a post-synthesis project; Tick the box "Do not specify sources at this time";
      Select part 'xc7a100tcsg324-1' 

      Open hadware manager and open taregt(xc7a100tcsg324-1). Program the device with .bit file generated above (vivado -mode ...)
      << you should see that 3 leds toggelling.
      
   -- gtkterm &; configure (19200 baud, 8bit, 1 stop bit, no parity and no flow control, USB1 port)
      << what ever key you type gets printed on the terminal and also 4th led toggles
   --
3.
